    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d87-a1">

                <pb facs="0212" n="202" sameAs="frus:frus1864p1/pg202"/>

                <head>Mr. Adams to Earl
                        Russell.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United
                                States,</hi><hi rendition="#italic"> London,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-02-22"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >February</hi> 22, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Lord:</hi> I beg permission to submit to your
                    consideration a copy of a journal called The Index, published in the interest
                    and under the direction of the emissaries of the insurgents in London. On page
                    107 of this number there appears what purports to be a letter from a person who
                    was engaged in the enterprise started in Canada to invade a portion of the
                    territory of the United States. It would seem, from the admissions made by this
                    individual, that the effort to make Canada the basis of an attack had been fully
                    sanctioned by the so-called authorities at Richmond, under the pretence of
                    exercising the right of passage through the territory. It is almost needless to
                    point out to your lordship the fraudulent character of these operations, a
                    feature so generally perceptible in the proceedings of these same parties in
                    foreign countries.</p>
                <p>I pray your lordship to accept the assurances of the highest consideration with
                    which I have the honor to be, my lord, your most obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>CHARLES FRANCIS ADAMS.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Right Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Earl Russell,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">&amp;c</hi>.<hi rendition="#italic">, &amp;c.,
                            &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>


                <xi:include href="d87-a1-a1.xml" xpointer="d87-a1-a1"/>
